        },
        "quote": "On receipt of the completed application form and the required fee, the City Manager or a designee shall determine whether the application is complete and sufficient for review, and whether the applicant’s business is eligible for an exemption under the State Constitution, this chapter and any other applicable laws. If the application is incomplete, the City Manager or a designee shall immediately notify the applicant, noting the need for such changes or additions as deemed necessary. If questions arise as to whether the business is legally eligible for an exemption, the matter shall be referred to the City Attorney, who shall consult with the applicant. If the application is found complete, and is for a purpose which appears to be authorized by law, the City Manager or a designee shall so notify the administrative review committee. (Ord. 18477 § 17, 7-12-05; Ord. 18365 § 2, 12-21-04; Ord. 17270 § 3, 6-2-98; Ord. 16349 § 3, 7-23-91. Code 1981 § 42-33. Code 1995 § 138-78.)",
